.SH NAME
.PP
jsonFormat\- Set BSON output format.When out of memory error happen, we can use
jsonFormat( false ) to disable BSON formatted output.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]jsonFormat(<pretty>)\f[]
.SH CATEGORY
.PP
Global
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Set BSON output format.
.SH PARAMETERS
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[C]pretty\f[] ( \f[I]Bool\f[], \f[I]Required\f[] * )
.PP
The flags of BSON formatted output.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.PP
NULL.
.SH HISTORY
.PP
Since v2.6
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP "1." 3
Use jsonFormat( false ) to disable BSON formatted output.
.nf
\f[C]
>\ db.foo.bar.find()
{
\ \ "_id":\ {
\ \ "$oid":\ "59fac185e610b8510e000001"
\ \ },
\ \ "a":\ 1,
\ \ "b":\ 2
}
Return\ 1\ row(s).
Takes\ 0.024873s.
>\ jsonFormat(\ false\ )
Takes\ 0.000225s.
>\ db.foo.bar.find()
{\ "_id":\ {\ "$oid":\ "59fac185e610b8510e000001"\ },\ "a":\ 1,\ "b":\ 2\ }
Return\ 1\ row(s).
Takes\ 0.002948s.
